                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "926b3426-5d7a-3841-abbb-5d17d646efe6",
                        "entry_id": "fb538b5f-bbd8-3476-b4c6-4a3b5bae9034",
                        "glosses": [
                            "в традиционном мусульманском быту — предмет женской одежды, покрывало, закрывающее всё туловище и лицо, кроме глаз и носа"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "49edddb4-cf7a-4b4c-a8ae-6cb97e827958",
                        "source_entry_id": "fb538b5f-bbd8-3476-b4c6-4a3b5bae9034",
                        "source_sense_id": "926b3426-5d7a-3841-abbb-5d17d646efe6",
                        "target_lang_word": "chador",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chador",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34f2c381-32db-376c-95b5-373bfeb2128e",
                                        "entry_id": "c02f34d5-33d6-32f2-bcac-87f195cafacb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A loose robe made from a single cloth, worn as a combination head covering, veil and shawl by chiefly Muslim women (and occasionally by those of other faiths) in Iran and South Asia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7487f98e-867c-4a22-af6b-468ff09fea33",
                                                "sense_id": "34f2c381-32db-376c-95b5-373bfeb2128e",
                                                "text": "Holonym: hijab"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ce7c377-40cb-4189-b9a8-e4809e219dd9",
                                                "sense_id": "34f2c381-32db-376c-95b5-373bfeb2128e",
                                                "text": "The Commodities are infinite: […] Pintados, Chints and Chadors, Shashes and Girdles, Cannakens[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48e180ea-59b0-453e-bc96-b36be28894ed",
                                                "sense_id": "34f2c381-32db-376c-95b5-373bfeb2128e",
                                                "text": "If those tablets were in Arabia, I'd put on a chador and burn my driver's licence and go there."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6125958d-1b98-4301-bf10-6e083d14cd71",
                                                "sense_id": "34f2c381-32db-376c-95b5-373bfeb2128e",
                                                "text": "The first few times Dolly stepped out into the city, cloaked by a chaddar that impaired her vision, she intuitively grabbed Sekond Lal's hand."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7c6a7092-4f0d-4a40-9925-346c59661282",
                        "source_entry_id": "fb538b5f-bbd8-3476-b4c6-4a3b5bae9034",
                        "source_sense_id": "926b3426-5d7a-3841-abbb-5d17d646efe6",
                        "target_lang_word": "tchador",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tchador",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41fef84c-426c-36b4-9b3d-82964ba26b86",
                                        "entry_id": "474a2550-fd0b-3f93-89c0-80740ae9701c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pièce de tissu semicirculaire ouverte sur le devant, portée traditionnellement par les femmes iraniennes et dans quelques pays d'Asie centrale, tenue en place avec les mains, les dents, ou une pince."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cb23b44-1542-42cd-b89c-3cb87c168b05",
                                                "sense_id": "41fef84c-426c-36b4-9b3d-82964ba26b86",
                                                "text": "Pour les musulmanes, le tchador peut se porter en plus du foulard pour compléter le hijab."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "734d634a-e708-4204-afa6-072b7d2150a4",
                                                "sense_id": "41fef84c-426c-36b4-9b3d-82964ba26b86",
                                                "text": "— J’y serai !\n— J’y serai !\n— Dussé-je vendre ma dernière brebis !\n— Mon dernier outil !\n— Le tchador de ma femme !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "978ae369-3125-42c3-b137-ed5034c5faf8",
                                                "sense_id": "41fef84c-426c-36b4-9b3d-82964ba26b86",
                                                "text": "À travers la fente ménagée dans la cagoule du tchador, les femmes, dont aucune, jamais, depuis les siècles qu’il se pratiquait, n’avait eu permission d’assister au jeu de tout un peuple, les suivaient d’un regard plein de rêves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89c66a18-ee86-437b-b904-a8013eb78ad0",
                                                "sense_id": "41fef84c-426c-36b4-9b3d-82964ba26b86",
                                                "text": "Ce voile a connu, en arabe ou en persan, de nombreux noms et d'innombrables formes, masquant plus ou moins le visage et le corps. du hidjab au tchador, ces variantes s'appuient toutes sur un incontestable fondement coranique."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
